{
 "duration": 42.955,
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "l1",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He said no to an order for a hundred thousand radios.",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 3.877
  },
  {
   "id": "l2",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "America, 1955. Akio Morita was selling a tiny radio from a small Japanese company called Sony.",
   "start": 4.097,
   "end": 12.383
  },
  {
   "id": "l3",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "According to Morita, a big American watch company wanted a hundred thousand of them.",
   "start": 12.603,
   "end": 17.758
  },
  {
   "id": "l4",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "A giant order for a tiny company. With one condition.",
   "start": 17.978,
   "end": 21.52
  },
  {
   "id": "l5",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The radios would carry the buyer's name. Not Sony's.",
   "start": 21.74,
   "end": 25.062
  },
  {
   "id": "l6",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Back in Tokyo, his board told him to take the deal.",
   "start": 25.282,
   "end": 28.668
  },
  {
   "id": "l7",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Morita refused. In fifty years, he said, our name will be as famous as yours.",
   "start": 28.888,
   "end": 34.196
  },
  {
   "id": "l8",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Sony became one of the best-known brands on Earth.",
   "start": 34.416,
   "end": 37.237
  },
  {
   "id": "l9",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Never rent out your name.",
   "start": 37.457,
   "end": 38.903
  },
  {
   "id": "l10",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "So, would you have taken the money? Or said no?",
   "start": 39.123,
   "end": 41.755
  }
 ],
